export anchor ExecutiveLargeStyle:
    number: 206
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Executive large
    idea: A dashboard built for a thirty second read by a manager, with 18px text, huge numbers, one idea per row and lots of air.
    base: light
    palette:
        linen: #f6f5f2, the page background and resting rows
        white: #ffffff, cards, the top bar and the style sheet
        ink: #1a1d1c, text and big numbers
        slate: #555b59, labels and secondary lines
        forest: #0d5c4a, the primary button, links, progress, focus and this week bars
        sage: #e3efeb, the current nav pill, activity avatars and a focused row
        lichen: #b5c9c3, last week bars, never text
        green: #1b6b3f, On track on #e6f2ea with a circle and check
        amber: #8a4f00, At risk on #fbf0dd with a triangle and bang
        red: #ab2328, Behind and the overdue callout on #fcecea with an octagon and bar
    type:
        One stack, Inter, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue,
        Arial, sans-serif. Base text is 18px at 1.55. The greeting is 56px
        at weight 750 tracked minus 0.025em, the overdue number 64px extra
        bold, KPI values 52px, project percents 44px, section titles 32px
        bold, card titles 24px bold and labels 17px in slate.
    layout:
        A white top bar holds the brand with a rounded forest tile, the six
        nav links as soft pills with Home filled sage, and on the right a
        pill New project button, a round bell and a round dark avatar.
        Under it a full width rounded search bar with a soft shadow. The
        hero row has the date and name above a 56px greeting on the left
        and a red tinted callout on the right with a huge 4 and the words
        tasks are overdue. Next, four tall white KPI tiles in one row.
        Then a section titled Where projects stand with the status counts
        on the right, and six project cards in a three by two grid, each
        with a status pill, a 24px name, the team, a 44px percent with the
        task count, a thick round progress bar and the due date with days
        left. Then a wide chart card with the week totals large on the
        left, 73 with Up 14 on last week over a smaller 59, and on the
        right fourteen rounded bars in two groups with each value printed
        on top. Last, Recent activity as a two column list with initials
        in sage circles. Below 1000px nav moves under the brand and grids
        go two wide. On phones everything is one column with KPIs two by
        two.
    spacing: An 8px unit in large steps. 24px gaps, 28px card padding and 64px between sections.
    density: Low. Six project cards and no table. The dashboard fits in about two screens.
    corners: 20px cards, 14 to 16px fields and rows, full pills for buttons, nav and chips.
    borders: Almost none. Hairlines only under the top bar and between activity rows.
    shadows: One soft lift on cards and the search bar, 0 8px 24px at 7 percent ink.
    icons:
        24px outline icons at 1.75px stroke. Status pills carry a filled
        circle with a white check, a filled triangle with a white bang, or
        a filled octagon with a white bar, plus the word.
    focus: A 3px forest outline offset 3px on every control, fields and rows included.
    tone: Plain sentences a manager would say aloud, such as Where projects stand and Up 14 on last week.
